---
import Footer from '@/components/Footer/Footer.astro'
import Header from '@/components/Header/Header.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader/PageHeader.astro'
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title='Accessibility Statement - The Lenders'
  description='The Lenders is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. Learn about our accessibility features and commitment.'
>
  <Header />

  <main class='main'>
    <PageHeader title='Accessibility Statement' />

    <section style='padding-block: clamp(3rem, 4vw, 5rem); background-color: var(--color-white); color: var(--color-blue-500);'>
      <style>
        .accessibility-list {
          list-style: none;
          padding-left: 0;
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          gap: 0.75rem;
        }
        .accessibility-list li {
          position: relative;
          padding-left: 2rem;
        }
        .accessibility-list li::before {
          content: '✓';
          position: absolute;
          left: 0;
          color: var(--color-gold-400);
          font-weight: bold;
          font-size: 1.25rem;
        }
      </style>
      <div class='container' style='max-width: 920px;'>
        <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem;'>
          <div>
            <h2>Our Commitment to Accessibility</h2>
            <p>
              The Lenders is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. 
              We are continually improving the user experience for everyone and applying the relevant 
              accessibility standards to ensure we provide equal access to all of our users.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Conformance Status</h2>
            <p>
              We strive to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level AA. 
              These guidelines explain how to make web content more accessible for people with disabilities 
              and more user-friendly for everyone.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Accessibility Features</h2>
            <p>Our website includes the following accessibility features:</p>
            <ul class='accessibility-list' style='margin-top: 1rem;'>
              <li>Semantic HTML markup for better screen reader compatibility</li>
              <li>Keyboard navigation support throughout the site</li>
              <li>Alternative text for images and graphics</li>
              <li>Clear heading structure for easy navigation</li>
              <li>Sufficient color contrast ratios for text and interactive elements</li>
              <li>Responsive design that works across different devices and screen sizes</li>
              <li>Forms with proper labels and error messages</li>
              <li>Skip navigation links for keyboard users</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
            <p>
              Despite our best efforts to ensure accessibility, there may be some limitations. 
              We are actively working to identify and address any accessibility barriers on our website.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Third-Party Content</h2>
            <p>
              Some pages on our website may contain content provided by third parties. While we strive 
              to ensure all content meets accessibility standards, we cannot always control the accessibility 
              of third-party content.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Feedback</h2>
            <p>
              We welcome your feedback on the accessibility of The Lenders website. If you encounter 
              accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, please contact us:
            </p>
            <ul class='accessibility-list' style='margin-top: 1rem;'>
              <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href='mailto:accessibility@thelenders.com' style='color: var(--color-blue-400); text-decoration: underline;'>accessibility@thelenders.com</a></li>
              <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href='tel:1-800-123-4567' style='color: var(--color-blue-400); text-decoration: underline;'>1-800-123-4567</a></li>
            </ul>
            <p style='margin-top: 1rem;'>
              We aim to respond to accessibility feedback within 5 business days and to provide 
              a solution or alternative within 10 business days.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Technical Specifications</h2>
            <p>
              The accessibility of The Lenders website relies on the following technologies to work 
              with the particular combination of web browser and any assistive technologies or plugins 
              installed on your computer:
            </p>
            <ul class='accessibility-list' style='margin-top: 1rem;'>
              <li>HTML5</li>
              <li>CSS3</li>
              <li>JavaScript</li>
              <li>ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Assessment and Testing</h2>
            <p>
              The Lenders assesses the accessibility of its website through:
            </p>
            <ul class='accessibility-list' style='margin-top: 1rem;'>
              <li>Self-evaluation and internal testing</li>
              <li>Automated accessibility testing tools</li>
              <li>Manual testing with assistive technologies</li>
              <li>User feedback and reports</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2>Date</h2>
            <p>
              This accessibility statement was last reviewed and updated on <strong>November 17, 2025</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style='padding: 1.5rem; background-color: rgba(0, 71, 171, 0.05); border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 1rem;'>
            <p style='margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;'>
              <strong>Note:</strong> We are continuously working to improve the accessibility of our website. 
              This statement reflects our ongoing commitment and will be updated as we make improvements.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

